WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:16.018
Unit eighteen: Sentence Transformation. Today you will rewrite a sentence so that it keeps the same meaning.

4
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:18.842
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.986
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.781
Transform.

7
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:28.282
Transform means to change the form of something.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.244
Transform the sentence.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.212
Your turn. Say: Transform.

10
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.254
Transform.

11
00:00:38.017 --> 00:00:38.971
Same meaning.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:43.028
Same meaning means meaning that does not change.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:44.896
Keep the same meaning.

14
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:48.321
Your turn. Say: Same meaning.

15
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.307
Same meaning.

16
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:53.981
Passive.

17
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:58.016
Passive means a form with be + past participle.

18
00:00:58.617 --> 00:01:00.117
Change to the passive.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:03.427
Your turn. Say: Passive.

20
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:06.896
Passive.

21
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.651
Reported.

22
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.021
Reported means told in other words.

23
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.361
Use reported speech.

24
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.521
Your turn. Say: Reported.

25
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.252
Reported.

26
00:01:22.017 --> 00:01:22.971
Conditional.

27
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.437
Conditional means with if.

28
00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.376
Use a conditional.

29
00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.357
Your turn. Say: Conditional.

30
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.201
Conditional.

31
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:35.939
Not as ... as.

32
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.286
Not as ... as means a comparison pattern.

33
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:41.465
She is not as tall as me.

34
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.772
Your turn. Say: Not as ... as.

35
00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:48.600
Not as ... as.

36
00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.316
Although.

37
00:01:51.317 --> 00:01:53.514
Although means in spite of the fact that.

38
00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:55.780
Although it rained, we played.

39
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:58.467
Your turn. Say: Although.

40
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.334
Although.

41
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:03.933
Too ... to.

42
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.600
Too ... to means more than is allowed or possible.

43
00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:10.032
It is too hot to go out.

44
00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:13.153
Your turn. Say: Too ... to.

45
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.769
Too ... to.

46
00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:21.229
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:24.675
Visal, what is a sentence transformation?

48
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:37.631
You get a sentence and the beginning of another, and you complete the new sentence so that it means the same. For example, She is taller than me becomes I am not as tall as her.

49
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:40.368
What structures are common?

50
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:52.109
Passive voice, reported speech, conditionals, comparatives, too and enough, although and but, and the present perfect with since and for.

51
00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:54.705
What is the best method?

52
00:02:55.817 --> 00:03:06.666
Read the first sentence and identify the structure. Then use the matching structure in the second sentence, and check that the meaning, tense and spelling are correct.

53
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.474
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.317 --> 00:03:15.056
Grammar focus: Strategy: identify the structure, then rewrite.

55
00:03:15.356 --> 00:03:16.589
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:20.699
She is taller than me → I am not as tall as her.

57
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:25.545
It was so cold that we stayed home → It was too cold to go out.

58
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:33.100
Identify the structure in the first sentence, then use a matching structure. Always check that the meaning and the grammar are correct.

59
00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:37.884
Be careful! Don't say: I change the meaning of the sentence.

60
00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:41.705
Say: I keep the same meaning.

61
00:03:42.005 --> 00:03:42.902
Same meaning.

62
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.364
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.760
Rewriting Sentences.

64
00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.348
Dara reads: The test was so difficult that nobody finished it.

65
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.646
He sees that the structure is so ... that.

66
00:03:56.633 --> 00:03:59.655
He rewrites it as: The test was too difficult to finish.

67
00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.643
He checks that the meaning is the same.

68
00:04:03.633 --> 00:04:05.900
He also checks the tense and the spelling.

69
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.338
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:12.183 --> 00:04:14.740
A transformation must keep the same blank.

71
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.694
A, meaning. B, length. C, number of words only.

72
00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:23.803
The answer is A: meaning.

73
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.019
She is taller than me. → I am blank tall as her.

74
00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:32.833
A, less. B, not as. C, as not.

75
00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.250
The answer is B: not as.

76
00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:40.952
Too hot blank go out.

77
00:04:41.252 --> 00:04:44.197
A, for. B, than. C, to.

78
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:49.408
The answer is C: to.

79
00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.213
What should you check at the end?

80
00:04:52.513 --> 00:04:56.573
A, meaning and grammar. B, your handwriting only. C, nothing.

81
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.841
The answer is A: meaning and grammar.

82
00:05:03.983 --> 00:05:07.155
The new sentence uses the same blank in a different form.

83
00:05:07.455 --> 00:05:11.434
A, title. B, idea. C, words exactly.

84
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.116
The answer is B: idea.

85
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.335
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:22.183 --> 00:05:24.473
How do you rewrite a sentence with the same meaning?

87
00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:35.027
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:35.327 --> 00:05:48.420
I identify the structure of the first sentence, such as comparison or passive. Then I choose a matching structure for the second sentence. Finally I check the meaning, the tense and the spelling.

89
00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.673
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:57.661
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: identify the structure, then rewrite.

91
00:05:57.961 --> 00:06:03.086
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:03.386 --> 00:06:05.876
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.176 --> 00:06:09.350
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

